This is great, but is there a way to do it without needing to redefine and hardcode any functions?

Ive tried various versions of this to no avail

```
    config = function()
      local files = require('mini.files')
      files.setup({
        mappings = {
          go_in = '',
          go_in_plus = '<C-l>',
          go_out = '',
          go_out_plus = '<C-h>',
        }
      })

      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {
        pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',
        callback = function(args)
          vim.keymap.set('n', '<CR>', function() files.go_in_plus() end, { buffer = args.data.buf_id })
        end,
      })
    end,
```

